## Why This Is Asked
New angle on CBA: gating cross‑app features via an on‑device policy engine, balancing UX, energy, and safety with cloud updates.

## Key Concepts
- On‑device policy engines and gating rules
- Resource awareness (battery, thermal, memory)
- Telemetry footprint and privacy compliance
- Rollout strategy and break‑even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRunFeature(state, policy) {
  if (state.battery < 20) return false;
  if (state.temperature > 45) return false;
  if (state.freeMemory < 200) return false;
  return policy.allowsFeature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify risk of safety incidents vs false positives?
- What metrics would drive policy update cadence and rollouts across device generations?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to quantify edge privacy investments, regulatory costs, and business impact for a real-world data minimization feature across Cloudflare/Snowflake contexts.

## Key Concepts
- Edge data minimization and on-device processing
- Local aggregation and secure delta encoding
- Regulatory risk, data residency, and cost-of-change trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function deltaEncode(events) {
  // Simplified delta-encoding by event type counts
  const counts = {};
  for (const e of events) {
    counts[e.type] = (counts[e.type] || 0) + 1;
  }
  return counts;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure energy impact across iOS/Android devices during rollout?
- What governance and testing would you implement for key rotation and revocation in clients?

